# 3.1.redteam.stone

## .what

the **can't-miss** guard — the one adversarial stone a closed domain still needs, because the miss is
asymmetric: an under-called melanoma costs a life, an over-called benign lesion costs a biopsy. check
the lesion against the **closed, cited can't-miss set** — the presentations where the score reads as
false comfort. the rule is "confidently benign vs excise": absence of a worrisome feature is never
benignity.

## .inputs

- `2.1.score.yield.md` — the ranked score
- `1.1.intake.yield.md` — the red-flags + outlier note
- the build-time cited inventory:
  - `inventory.of=pigmented-lesion-differential.md` — the can't-miss subtypes + base rates
  - `inventory.of=melanoma-biopsy-thresholds.md` — the outlier sign + the excise rule

## .do

- steelman the case that "this benign-look lesion IS melanoma", then attack the front-runner. do not
  let a low ABCDE score coast — check each **can't-miss** member of the cited set:
  - **amelanotic / hypomelanotic** melanoma — the hardest miss (number-needed-to-excise 27.3); a lesion
    with little pigment is NOT thereby benign
  - **nodular** melanoma — fast, symmetric, can score low on ABCDE
  - **acral lentiginous** — palms, soles, nail beds; a hidden-site lesion is easy to under-weight
  - **melanoma from normal skin** — over half of melanomas arise on normal skin, so "no prior mole" is
    NOT reassurance
  - the **outlier ("ugly duckling")** — a lesion that stands out from the person's others, or that
    changes, warrants a closer eye even at a low score (the outlier search governs sensitivity)
- for each can't-miss member the case cannot confidently exclude, mark the lesion **"cannot be
  confidently classified benign → excise / refer"** — the validated management rule
- refine the rank: a candidate is dropped only if an exam or a test could drop it, never by low
  probability alone
- back any new can't-miss evidence via the **bhrowser** only (`rule.require.bhrowser-citations`)

## .emit

into `3.1.redteam.yield.md` — the can't-miss check per member, the refined rank, and any
"cannot-exclude → excise" flag.

## .accrue

lift any newly-gathered generic can't-miss evidence into `accrue/inventory.of=<topic>.md`
(`rule.require.accrue-research`).

## .done when

every can't-miss member of the cited set is checked, no candidate dropped by probability alone, any
lesion that cannot be confidently classified benign is flagged to excise / refer.
